# Per-file line-coverage floors, enforced by scripts/check-coverage.sh.
#
# The aggregate gate in .coverage-threshold can pass while one module sits far below the
# line and another sits near 100%. These floors catch that (#643).
#
# Format: <repo-relative path> <floor percent>
#
# The "*" entry is the floor for any file with no entry of its own, so a new module added
# without tests fails the gate rather than passing unnoticed.
#
# Each floor sits a couple of points below where the file measured when it was written, so
# a refactor that moves a line or two does not fail the build. Raise a floor when the
# script reports the file sitting well above it — never lower one to make CI pass.
#
# main.rs and telemetry.rs carry honest low floors rather than being dropped from the
# report. Excluding a file inflates the number by measuring less code (#71).

